{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/16161-horror-recognition-guide-10-pictures","id":16161,"title":"Horror Recognition Guide: 10 Pictures","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-11-22T10:19:16-08:00","id":16161,"title":"Horror Recognition Guide: 10 Pictures","content":"Okay, I have to ask: what is this stuff in HRG's 10 Pictures chapter? It was deliciously creepy, but I'm not sure which part of WoD this chapter presents. Is that supposed to be the spirit world?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1245-varsovian","name":"Varsovian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-22T10:39:15-08:00","id":16171,"title":"","content":"They sold the Collection of Horrors stuff alongside it. All it explains, however, is that they are &quot;alternative geographies.&quot;<br /> <br /> To be specific, &quot;Somewhere in the wretched tangle of streets, buildings and people, pockets of unreality build up until they fill up with some other place like pus into a blister.&quot;<br /> <br /> I suppose it would fit as aspects of the Hedge, even Arcadia, the Shadow, another world, Infrastructure, the Abyss, or anything else.<br /> <br /> I hope it was put in as an example of new situations that aren't specifically tied to other splats (because there is more in the World of Darkness than described in the books).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 11-22-2013, 01:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-22T11:31:25-08:00","id":16201,"title":"","content":"I got the impression it was of the Prince of 100,000 Leaves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-22T12:02:49-08:00","id":16218,"title":"","content":"And what is the Prince of 100,000 Leaves?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1245-varsovian","name":"Varsovian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-22T13:12:03-08:00","id":16250,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Varsovian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/16161-horror-recognition-guide-10-pictures?p=16218#post16218\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And what is the Prince of 100,000 Leaves?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi, on the old forums</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">So, just to clarify the previous points, the Prince of 100,000 Leaves is an alternate history where a particularly terrible Egyptian cult grew powerful enough to alter the course of the world, creating a world where atrocities are committed on a daily basis, cannibalism is revered as the most sacred of acts, and all great cities are enormous temples to mad gods constructed from the bones of sacrificial victims who died (and continue to die) in unspeakable agony. It was so abharrant that it was aborted from reality into the Abyss, where it became sentient (the sentience personified by the name Prince of 100,000 Leaves, among others) and began actively seeking to enter reality. The means through which it can do so is to manifest fragments the pages of its entire history that were compiled by an insane Egyptian priest thousands of years ago. If the full history of the Prince is compiled in the Fallen World, than it will overwrite history. It is actively worshipped by the Red Word, a cult of mad cannibals who seek out the fragments. Gathering fragments together can cause certain manifestations from the anti-history to appear, like spirits of balefire, spirits of cannibalism which are regal rather than feral, and temples for the Red Word.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-22T13:41:54-08:00","id":16261,"title":"","content":"The add-ons for the Horrir Recognition guide describe it as &quot;intersitial terrain,&quot; places where other realities occupy the same space as our own. I think the implication was that this is where Cheiron's inhuman Board of Directors comes from.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-22T13:55:12-08:00","id":16271,"title":"","content":"Wait, which add-ons? Have I missed something?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1245-varsovian","name":"Varsovian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-22T14:23:03-08:00","id":16277,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/16161-horror-recognition-guide-10-pictures?p=16261#post16261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The add-ons for the Horrir Recognition guide describe it as &quot;intersitial terrain,&quot; places where other realities occupy the same space as our own. I think the implication was that this is where Cheiron's inhuman Board of Directors comes from.</div> </div> </div> </div>Difficult to say, since interstitial terrain also shows up in Shadows of the U.K. with slightly different time constraints and a suggestion that the particular instances detailed in that book are a result of a very crowded Shadow \u2014 the Other City in Glasgow is apparently one huge Verge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-22T14:45:54-08:00","id":16290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Varsovian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/16161-horror-recognition-guide-10-pictures?p=16271#post16271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue anim